Blobby Volley 2 @VERSION@ for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
==========================================================

Blobby Volley 2 is volleyball for two: two blobs, a net and a beach ball.
Play a friend on one keyboard or one of the six bots. The first to 15
points wins, and only the serving side scores. This is its AmigaOS 3.x
build for a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, with SDL 2 through GFOpenGPU.
The game's graphics, sounds and bots are in the drawer: it plays as it
comes.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU (not an LC040 or EC040),
  AmiCradle or an RTG board with an 800x600 screen mode.
- GFOpenGPU with SDL2.module and SDL2_mixer.module in LIBS:GFOpenGPU/
  (from gfopenrtg's main of 2 November 2026 or later).
- AHI for sound (OpenAHI's driver on AmiCradle).

Installing
----------

OS 3.2 has no lha command: unpack the archive with OpenCompress (on
AmiCradle, SYS:Utilities/OpenCompress), for example into RAM:

  OpenCompress x blobbyvolley2-@VERSION@-68040.lha RAM:

Then open RAM: and double-click Install-BlobbyVolley2. The Amiga
Installer checks for a 68040 or 68060 with its FPU, asks for the drawer
to put BlobbyVolley2 in (Work:Games is offered), makes sure
LIBS:GFOpenGPU has SDL2.module and SDL2_mixer.module (copying them from
LIBS:OpenGPU when only that has them, as on an older AmiCradle), and
copies the game. The game writes only in the User drawer it makes beside
itself (its settings and saved replays); run the Installer again to
update, and User is left as it is.

Playing
-------

- The game's icon opens an 800x600 screen of its own. Options, Graphic
  Options, Window Mode puts it in a window on the Workbench instead.
- Start plays a match with the players set in Options: on the left a
  person, on the right a person or a bot (Union, Axji, Com 11,
  Gintonic, Hyp014, Reduced), each bot at the strength chosen there.
- Watch Replay plays a replay saved from a match (Escape, Save Replay).
- From a Shell: cd to the drawer, then blobby. blobby NAME BOT.lua (or
  two names) starts a match at once and quits when it ends. -fps writes
  the frame rate each second.

Controls
--------

Keyboard (upstream's defaults): the left player moves with A and D and
jumps with W; the right player moves with the cursor keys and jumps with
Up. Escape pauses a match (Yes quits it). In the menus, the mouse, or the
cursor keys and Return.

Options, Input Options sets a keyboard, the mouse or a joystick for each
player. Joystick for the left player is the stick or CD32 pad in port 2
(left and right to move, fire to jump); for the right player a stick in
port 1. A CD32 pad's Play is Escape. Stick and pad play has not been
tried on real hardware yet.

